  "releaseNotes": "- [ThunderPropagator#70] [Performance] Subscription matching is O(n) per message — replace linear scan with inverted index for O(1) keyed-subscription lookup   ---   Removed _subscribedKeys (ConcurrentDictionary<SubscribedKeys, HashSet<int>>)   The only purpose it served after PR #70 was as the source for the Remove(string, IReadOnlyDictionary) O(n) scan. That method now uses _requestIds to get candidates (O(k) where k = subscriptions   per requestId), then checks SubscribedKeys.Equals() on that small set — same correctness, no dedicated secondary index needed.\\n- [ThunderPropagator#70] [Performance] Subscription matching is O(n) per message — replace linear scan with inverted index for O(1) keyed-subscription lookup   - AddToIndex: walks the SubscribedKeys enumerator (yields descriptorName:value pairs), inserts the key into _index[fieldName:value]. Zero-key subscriptions go into _broadcastSubscribedKeys.   - RemoveFromIndex: mirrors add — removes the key from each bucket, drops empty buckets from _index.   - MakeIndexKey: $'{fieldName}:{value}' — same format used on both the subscription side and the message side at lookup time.   - SearchInSubscribedKeys: unions all matching SubscribedKeys sets from the index across every message field, appends broadcast subscriptions, then applies the exact IsEquals check on the candidate    set only — typically O(k) where k ≪ n.",
